{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZmBEYySdnriV3YprBCP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I proved node-search monotonicity in Lean, so the named gap `NodeSearchMonotonicity` is now a theorem. That completes item 14 and the loop (14/14). The gate passes (`lake build`, 1,231 tests, sorry count unchanged at the baseline 1, no new axioms), and nothing is committed.\n\n**What's proved** (two new files, no `sorry`, and only the three standard axioms):\n- **`Complex/NodeMonotonicity.lean`**:\n  - `nodeSearchMonotonicity`: recontamination does not help, on every finite graph.\n  - `ns = vs + 1 = pw + 1` for the full game on graphs with an edge (Kirousis & Papadimitriou 1986, Theorem 4.1).\n  - `ns = θ` for the full game (their 1985 Theorem).\n  - `nodeSearch_chain`: `θ = ns = mns = vs + 1 = pw + 1`.\n  - Möhring's Theorem 3.9 for the full game.\n- **`Complex/EdgeSearchFull.lean`**: `vs ≤ es` for the full edge game. With the existing upper bound this gives Ellis, Sudborough & Turner's Theorem 2.1 (`vs ≤ es ≤ vs + 2`) as they state it, without assuming LaPaugh's theorem. It also gives `ns − 1 ≤ es ≤ ns + 1` for the full games.\n\n**How:** not the sources' route through LaPaugh's theorem. I used Bienstock & Seymour's crusade argument over vertex sets:\n1. The measure is each set's outer boundary (neighbours outside the set). That measure is submodular, and it is exactly what vertex separation counts at a prefix of a layout.\n2. A chain of sets with small boundaries can be rearranged into an increasing one, and an increasing chain reads off as a layout.\n3. Any search strategy, recontaminating or not, yields such a chain by tracking the vertices that touch no contaminated edge.\n\nThis never needs a recontamination-free strategy, so it also avoids the error in Kirousis & Papadimitriou's own proof.\n\n**Not done:** LaPaugh's `es = pes` (`EdgeSearchMonotonicity`) was not attempted and remains a named `Prop`. No row of the master table depends on it any more.\n\n**Docs updated:**\n- `paper2/equivalences.md`: rows 5–7, the tally, the gaps section, the census sections, and a new \"Item 14\" section.\n- The chain figure is redrawn.\n- `paper2/axiom_check.lean` now names 44 theorems, all clean.\n- `lean_repo_plan.md` now lists 13 files.\n- `PROGRESS.md` has the iteration entry and `LOOP_COMPLETE`, and `iterations.md` has the item checked.\n\nOne stale note: the rules forbid editing existing files, so `NodeSearch.lean`'s docstring still says the full game is unproved. That can be fixed when the Lean moves to the paper's repository."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1916,"cache_read_input_tokens":215806,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1916,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82059cc5-0efd-4d43-a543-b0f36ee7f79b","uuid":"52015c09-d6cc-443c-b977-3a69b10dba1d","timestamp":"2026-09-30T14:13:57.150Z","request_id":"req_011CfZmBE6SWZZXZAAcpePKA"}
